- **NEGATION DROPPED**: line 265.  
  Exact input: `pos_probe = "P"*40`; `pos_page = "P"*40 + " THIS SENTENCE IS IN NO OBJECT AND MUST NOT BE FOUND ANYWHERE"`.  
  Consequence: the negative control is satisfied when the forbidden sentence is present, so the guard is inverted.

- **SELECTOR KEYED TO WRONG FORM**: line 110.  
  Exact input: `refusal_named_in_section('<h3><span>Certainty of the evidence</span></h3><p>Refused:</p>', 'Certainty of the evidence')`.  
  Consequence: a refusal under a real heading with inline markup is reported as “the section heading is not on the page at all.”

- **SECTION BOUNDARY SELECTOR MATCHES TOO LITTLE**: line 115.  
  Exact input: `refusal_named_in_section('<h2>Certainty of the evidence</h2><p>No refusal here.</p><h2>Next section</h2><p>Refused:</p>', 'Certainty of the evidence')`.  
  Consequence: `Refused:` from the next `<h2>` section is counted as belonging to the prior limb section.

- **TEXT COMPARED RAW ACROSS LINE-ENDINGS**: line 311.  
  Exact input: `cand = "A"*40 + "\r\n" + "B"*40`; delivered page text contains `"A"*40 + "\n" + "B"*40`.  
  Consequence: equal rendered content is reported `HELD ONLY` because CRLF/LF normalization is absent.

- **CHECK CANNOT FAIL CLOSED**: lines 272-275.  
  Exact input: `ssot/bad/bad.json` containing `{` with basename matching topic directory.  
  Consequence: malformed SSOT input is silently dropped from the denominator instead of failing the audit.

